# SYNOPSIS

```ndb
match=pci vendor=0x1af4 device=0x1050 program=/boot/bin/drv-virtio-gpu
    post=display0 msi=1
```

# DESCRIPTION

`drv-virtio-gpu` drives a virtio GPU's 2D commands as a back end of the display engine protocol (docs/proto/display.md, ADR-0026) on `/srv/display0`, for displayd(8).
devmgr(8) starts it for a modern virtio GPU, with its configuration space, BARs, a DMA domain and one MSI-X interrupt.

The screen is one host resource the size of scanout 0's mode, which GET_DISPLAY_INFO gives.
An imported image stays in guest memory, given to the device through the DMA domain; applying it attaches it as the screen resource's backing, and the next vblank transfers the damage into the resource and flushes the damage to the display.
So it copies only what an APPLY says changed, as drv-simplefb(3) does.
A colour layer is an image of its own, filled with the colour.
An image's rows must be the screen resource's: those vx-buffer's layout gives the mode's width.

The output is reported in the device's mode, with its EDID (GET_EDID) unparsed, which displayd parses.
Its vblank is a timer at 60 Hz: virtio-gpu has neither a vblank nor a refresh rate.
Nothing the firmware showed survives the firmware's exit, so there is no picture to adopt or put back; a session that ends leaves the last picture showing.

